<title>USA: Magnum says 1996 proved reserves rise.</title>
<headline>Magnum says 1996 proved reserves rise.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magnum Petroleum Inc Thursday said its 1996 year-end proved oil and gas reserves increased 231 percent to 20.43 million barrels of oil equivalent, up from 6.18 million barrels at year-end 1995.</p>
<p>The company also said total proved natural gas reserves increased for the year by 340 percent to 90.6 billion cubic feet from from 20.6 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>Total proved oil and liquids reserves increased 29 percent from 4.1 million barrels to 5.3 million barrels, the company said.</p>
